Bundled Rust crates
------------------
The generated orig tarball contains the crates pinned by Cargo.lock and
the matching distro Rust library workspace's Cargo.lock,
including pmi, devtree and burrow from their pinned Git revisions. These
retain their upstream copyrights and licenses. LICENSE.dependencies
records each crate's name, version, declared license and authors, together
with the license and notice files supplied by that crate. It is generated
by debian/make-orig-source.py and installed alongside this file.

The linked runtime crates use Apache-2.0, MIT, or their declared alternative
licenses (including 0BSD, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, Unlicense and Zlib).
The vendor tree also includes build, test and other-platform dependencies;
their license declarations and supplied notices are recorded there too.

Rust bare-metal libraries
------------------------
The build also compiles core and compiler_builtins from the distro rust-src
package and embeds them in tatu. These retain the Rust project's MIT and
Apache-2.0 licenses, including the LLVM exception for compiler_builtins.
Their source and license notices are supplied by the rust-src Build-Depends;
the distro's Rust copyright file is installed as copyright.rust-src.
